Done. Here's a summary of the component:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Renders items in a `<ul>` with "Move Up" / "Move Down" buttons per item. Buttons are disabled at the boundaries.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Generic `partial class` with:
- `Items` (`IReadOnlyList<TItem>`) — input list, never mutated
- `ItemTemplate` (`RenderFragment<TItem>`) — slot for rendering each item
- `OnOrderChanged` (`EventCallback<IReadOnlyList<TItem>>`) — fires after reorder with the new list
- Internal `_items` copy created in `OnParametersSet`

Usage matches your example:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private List<TaskItem> tasks = [...];

    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> updated)
    {
        tasks = updated.ToList();
    }
}
```
